From: pyvm <pyvm@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] riscv: place .got in the data section

Linux 6.1's riscv vmlinux.lds.S does not place the .got section.  When the
kernel is built with clang/lld, the GOT (used for weak symbols such as the
kallsyms tables) is placed by orphan rules between __init_begin and
__init_end, so it is freed by free_initmem().  Any later GOT load, e.g. in
kallsyms during a stack trace or /proc/kallsyms, then reads recycled memory
and hits "kernel BUG at kernel/kallsyms.c:335".

Place .got explicitly after .sdata so it lives in permanent data.
---
--- a/arch/riscv/kernel/vmlinux.lds.S	2026-09-30 15:01:33.705504409 +0800
+++ b/arch/riscv/kernel/vmlinux.lds.S	2026-09-30 15:01:33.721216461 +0800
@@ -122,6 +122,14 @@
 		*(.sdata*)
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * Keep the GOT in the permanent data section.  Clang emits GOT loads
+	 * for weak symbols (e.g. kallsyms_*); left to the linker's orphan
+	 * placement, .got ends up inside the init area and is freed after
+	 * boot, after which those loads read recycled memory.
+	 */
+	.got : { *(.got*) }
+
 #ifdef CONFIG_EFI
 	.pecoff_edata_padding : { BYTE(0); . = ALIGN(PECOFF_FILE_ALIGNMENT); }
 	__pecoff_data_raw_size = ABSOLUTE(. - __pecoff_text_end);
